ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: green
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "HuggingFace DataTrove", url: "https://github.com/huggingface/datatrove/blob/main/src/datatrove/utils/text.py", overlap: "Direct dedup-normalizer overlap; simplify_text lowercases and uses NFD+strip-Mn, not NFKC+casefold, matching the claimed open seam."},
  {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching/", overlap: "Caches by token/block hash after tokenization; token-aligned cache reuse, but not corpus near-dedup normalization alignment."},
  {system: "SGLang RadixAttention/RadixCache", url: "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/radix_cache.py", overlap: "RadixKey stores and matches token_ids; overlap is token-prefix cache identity, not pretraining dedup false negatives."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/lmcache/v1/token_database.py", overlap: "Hashes token ID chunks into cache keys; overlap is token-key canonicalization for KV cache, not text dedup normalization."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "Reuse depends on same prompt/input_ids and full token blocks; no evidence of NFKC/casefold-aware corpus dedup."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: Holds for the packet's stated workload: real C4 multilingual validation, 20,000 docs across 5 languages, 9,044 model-identical NFKC-twin pairs, residual_FN_rate 95.1%, and 34.6% of residual FNs still missed under production-style 5-gram char-shingle MinHash at T=0.8. Gaps: sample is validation-scale rather than full production crawl; GT is NFKC+casefold rather than a loaded tokenizer.json; artifact reproducibility depends on the EXP-0069 scripts and HF dataset-server availability.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. Prior-art check found shipping systems that either (1) expose the vulnerable dedup normalizer path, DataTrove lower+NFD+strip-Mn, or (2) operate after tokenization for KV/prefix cache reuse using token IDs. I found no shipping OSS system among DataTrove/vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/TensorRT-LLM/FlashInfer that implements the claimed mechanism for corpus near-dedup: aligning MinHash/shingle dedup normalization to the model tokenizer's Unicode equivalence classes. The contribution is not the known Unicode fact that NFKC compatibility decomposition differs from NFD; it is the measured systems failure mode at the dedup/tokenizer boundary: 8,605/9,044 model-identical real multilingual pairs escape the production default, with per-language rates zh 99.8%, ja 98.4%, de 94.7%, fr 94.6%, ar 55.6%. The obvious fix does not make this integration-only because the evidence shows current OSS defaults do not apply it and the residual is measured on real workload rather than a toy string example.
